Negative control for the FilterMultiSelectRenderer facet-write SEQUENCE fix
(FE-3031). Retargeted 2026-09-12: the original attacked
`form/engine/renderers/array/StringsRenderer.vue`, which the gitlab/develop
merge deleted when the form engine moved to the ui package. The compact bar
facet (`FilterMultiSelectRenderer.vue`) is that capability's home now, and
this patch attacks it at the same seam.

Assertion it attacks: the SEQUENCE on the wire, not a single click — driving
one status tile (click A), then a second (click B), then de-selecting the
first (click A again) must leave `translateQuery(schema, model())`'s
`filter[status.code|in]` carrying ONLY the still-selected value (click B's),
with no duplicate entries anywhere in the array at any step. A single click
never exercises a diff against prior selection, so an assertion on one click
passes clean while the sequence is broken underneath it.

The mutation: read the live selection from `control.value.data` instead of
resolving the leaf's own literal path off the injected core data. For a
filter column whose name carries a literal dot (`"status.code"`,
`"category.slug"` — the API's own names), `@jsonforms/core` joins the scope on
"." and splits it again, so it walks `data.filters.status.code` instead of
`data.filters["status.code"]` and `control.value.data` is PERMANENTLY
`undefined`. Every toggle then computes its next selection against an empty
current: a de-select can never remove, and a re-click can only re-add.

PROVING ASSERTION EXISTS YET: the permanent gate is
`packages/client-vue/src/components/form/renderers/__tests__/invoices-filter-wire.test.ts`,
whose two `the facet SEQUENCE never duplicates and de-select removes` cases
(one per dotted column) are the assertions this mutation must flip.

VERIFIED 2026-09-12: applied against the fixed source, `invoices-filter-wire.test.ts`
went 2 failed | 159 passed (161) — exactly the two SEQUENCE cases red, every
other assertion in the file still green, which is what makes this a control on
THIS capability rather than a broad breakage. Reverted immediately after; the
fixed source re-confirmed GREEN at 161/161.

--- a/packages/client-vue/src/components/form/renderers/FilterMultiSelectRenderer.vue
+++ b/packages/client-vue/src/components/form/renderers/FilterMultiSelectRenderer.vue
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 /** Read by literal path: `control.data` never resolves for a dotted column. */
 const selected = computed<unknown[]>(
-  () => get(jsonforms?.core?.data, literalPath.value) ?? []
+  () => (control.value.data as unknown[]) ?? []
 );
